  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Since the line lie in the plane, so&nbsp;<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4,2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;also lie in the plane and vector along the line is perpendicular to normal to the plane</p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math><mn>8</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math></p><p>Hence, the ordered pair is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>",
